# LeakSanitizer suppressions for serverNavGame
#
# Every entry here is a THIRD-PARTY leak (GPU driver / Vulkan loader / windowing /
# ASan runtime) reproduced by running ./game under ASan on lavapipe. None of these
# are application bugs. Verified 2026-07-08: the single frame that ASan attributed to
# "game+0x282b28" resolves past the binary's _end (0x10e5e8) -> it is the lavapipe
# JIT mis-attributed by ASan's fast frame-pointer unwinder, not real game code.
#
# A "leak:<substring>" entry suppresses a leak if the substring appears in ANY frame
# of its allocation stack (function name, source file, or module name). Because most
# driver frames only resolve to a MODULE name, run the audit with the slow unwinder
# (ASAN_OPTIONS=fast_unwind_on_malloc=0) so these module names actually appear.

# --- Vulkan loader ---
leak:libvulkan

# --- Mesa software Vulkan (lavapipe / llvmpipe) ICD, gallium, LLVM JIT ---
leak:libvulkan_lvp
leak:lvp_
leak:swrast
leak:libgallium
leak:libLLVM
leak:libdrm
leak:libglapi
leak:libvulkan_intel
leak:libvulkan_radeon

# --- X11 / XCB windowing (pulled in by GLFW) ---
leak:libxcb
leak:libX11
leak:libxcb-

# --- GLFW ---
leak:libglfw

# --- ASan / LSan runtime's own bookkeeping ---
leak:libasan
